00:47:55,000 --> 00:48:01,000
Ghostbusters: Frozen Empire is a 2024 American supernatural comedy film
directed by Gil Kenan, and written by Kenan and Jason Reitman.

11
00:52:42,500 --> 00:52:48,500
It is the fifth in the Ghostbusters film series.

12
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
The film features Paul Rudd, Carrie Coon, Finn Wolfhard and Mckenna Grace reprising their roles from the previous film, with Ernie Hudson
and Annie Potts reprising their characters from the earlier films, and Kumail Nanjiani and Patton Oswalt joining the cast.

13
01:02:17,500 --> 01:02:23,500
It sees the veteran Ghostbusters returning to New York City and collaborating
with their successors to save the world from a new ancient evil.

14
01:07:05,000 --> 01:07:11,000
Following the success of Ghostbusters: Afterlife, Sony Pictures announced
the sequel in April 2022, with Reitman returning as director.

15
01:11:52,500 --> 01:11:58,500
In December, co-writer and executive producer Kenan took over as
director, with Reitman remaining as co-writer and co-producer.

16
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
The same month, Rudd, Coon, Wolfhard, Grace, Hudson, Potts, Bill Murray and
Dan Aykroyd were all confirmed to be reprising their roles.

17
01:21:27,500 --> 01:21:33,500
New cast members including Nanjiani and Oswalt were announced in March 2023, with
principal photography commencing that month and wrapping in June.

18
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
Dario Marianelli composed the film's score.

19
01:31:02,500 --> 01:31:08,500
As the first film in the Ghostbusters franchise to be released following the death of the franchise's co-creator and Jason
Reitman's father Ivan Reitman, who posthumously receives credit as a producer, the film is dedicated to his memory.

20
01:35:50,000 --> 01:35:56,000
Ghostbusters: Frozen Empire had its premiere at the AMC Lincoln Square Theater in New York City on March
14, 2024, and was released in the United States on March 22 by Sony Pictures Releasing.

21
01:40:37,500 --> 01:40:43,500
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed
$202 million on a budget of $100 million.

22
